  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}\u2061x={sec}^{2}\u2061x\n$$\n\nAlso, recall the Pythagorean formula for sines and cosines:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above identities, we can simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x)+{tan}^{2}\u2061x & =1+{tan}^{2}\u2061x \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
